WEBVTT

1
00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.619
[Bobby]
<i>We're here for a reason.</i>

2
00:00:51.686 --> 00:00:55.023
<i>Put on this earth</i>
<i>for a higher purpose.</i>

3
00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.824
<i>I have to believe that.</i>

4
00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:59.126
<i>I have to believe</i>
<i>that there's a higher purpose</i>

5
00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:03.698
<i>for me being here on this</i>
<i>corner at this time of day.</i>

6
00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:06.834
<i>Looking at those</i>
<i>fucking doors again.</i>

7
00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.803
[James] <i>I'm worried</i>
<i>that you get too close.</i>

8
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.405
<i>-Yeah, I'm getting close.</i>
-Too close to that world.

9
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.943
You don't kill anybody. Don't
shoot him in the face, okay?

10
00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:16.644
Where's his fucking money?

11
00:01:16.711 --> 00:01:18.378
[screams]

12
00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:22.249
[Bobby] <i>But I'm early</i>
<i>and in no rush whatsoever</i>

13
00:01:22.316 --> 00:01:24.619
<i>to find</i>
<i>out what that purpose is.</i>

14
00:01:24.686 --> 00:01:27.154
<i>The why can wait, but the how,</i>

15
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.124
<i>that's actually a pretty</i>
<i>good story.</i>

16
00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.827
You tell them
you're an architect.

17
00:01:32.894 --> 00:01:35.128
You can go with a doctor
or a lawyer if you want,

18
00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.832
but I'm telling you
the chicks can somehow sniff
those out right away.

19
00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:39.567
Why don't you just
tell them the truth?

20
00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.301
The second
you tell them you're a cop,

21
00:01:41.368 --> 00:01:43.605
you can see the hamster wheel
start turning.

22
00:01:43.671 --> 00:01:45.707
They go through every
bad thing they've done,

23
00:01:45.773 --> 00:01:47.542
Wondering how it can be used
against them.

24
00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:50.277
So you tell them
that you're an architect.

25
00:01:50.344 --> 00:01:52.981
It's a desk job.
Relatable, safe,

26
00:01:53.047 --> 00:01:55.550
but distinguished enough.
Not scare them off.

27
00:01:55.617 --> 00:02:00.320
And architects make money,
so that helps.

28
00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:02.255
What happens when they find out
you're lying?

29
00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.290
Never happens.

30
00:02:03.357 --> 00:02:04.826
[radio chatter]

31
00:02:04.892 --> 00:02:07.795
I got to say, you know...

32
00:02:07.862 --> 00:02:12.033
Sounds good and all but I mean
dating sounds like a nightmare.

33
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.167
It is. You're a lucky man.

34
00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.738
Married to a great woman.

35
00:02:16.804 --> 00:02:19.641
Yeah...

36
00:02:19.707 --> 00:02:21.643
Trouble at home?

37
00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:23.911
Yeah.

38
00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:25.479
I don't want to talk about it.

39
00:02:25.546 --> 00:02:29.249
It's the job.
You need to find a balance.

40
00:02:30.752 --> 00:02:33.955
I used to buy her flowers,
you know, just because.

41
00:02:34.022 --> 00:02:36.758
And then it was only on
special occasions, right?

42
00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:38.793
But those became
too few to count,

43
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.360
and then it was only
when I fucked up,

44
00:02:40.427 --> 00:02:44.732
and, you know,
I fucked up a lot.

45
00:02:44.799 --> 00:02:46.801
So eventually, you know,

46
00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.771
flowers didn't mean
anything anymore,

47
00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:52.305
so I stopped.

48
00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.742
Sounds like you do
want to talk about it.

49
00:02:54.809 --> 00:02:58.613
Bobby, go back
home to your wife,

50
00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.916
get her some flowers
and get that balance back.

51
00:03:13.728 --> 00:03:14.829
Hey.

52
00:03:14.896 --> 00:03:15.897
Bobby.

53
00:03:15.963 --> 00:03:17.464
Shut your mouth.

54
00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:20.568
Hey, don't you talk
to her like that.

55
00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.338
Why don't you shut
your mouth too?

56
00:03:27.441 --> 00:03:29.811
I got you flowers.

57
00:03:31.713 --> 00:03:34.048
Maybe you should
just leave, man.

58
00:03:34.115 --> 00:03:40.021
[Bobby] <i>I should have taken</i>
<i>his advice. But instead...</i>

59
00:03:40.088 --> 00:03:41.622
Bobby, stop!

60
00:03:41.689 --> 00:03:43.825
[Bobby] <i>I decided to</i>
<i>redecorate my kitchen.</i>

61
00:03:43.891 --> 00:03:47.294
Stop! Stop.

62
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.230
Stop! Bobby, please, stop!

63
00:03:50.297 --> 00:03:52.834
[screaming]

64
00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.139
Please!

65
00:03:58.206 --> 00:03:59.507
[sobs]

66
00:03:59.574 --> 00:04:01.308
[groans]

67
00:04:20.995 --> 00:04:23.463
[Bobby] <i>There's a moment</i>
<i>right before you're fully awake</i>

68
00:04:23.531 --> 00:04:27.267
<i>where there's</i>
<i>a slight chance that you</i>
<i>could still be dreaming.</i>

69
00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:32.339
<i>And then comes the moment</i>
<i>when you realize you're not.</i>

70
00:04:33.875 --> 00:04:36.677
<i>I've been married</i>
<i>for almost ten years</i>

71
00:04:36.744 --> 00:04:39.680
<i>and a cop for almost twelve.</i>

72
00:04:39.747 --> 00:04:41.414
Well, how do you know that

73
00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:44.552
he doesn't have
a license for that?

74
00:04:44.619 --> 00:04:47.287
No, no, that's
because you think that.

75
00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:50.892
You think that. See, you
can't make assumptions.

76
00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:53.060
Yeah. Yeah.

77
00:04:53.127 --> 00:04:55.730
Hey, there's a fresh pot
over there if you're interested.

78
00:04:55.797 --> 00:04:59.567
I got to call you back.
Okay. Bye bye.

79
00:05:02.369 --> 00:05:04.071
You're going
to be here for a while,

80
00:05:04.138 --> 00:05:05.206
you should make the most of it.

81
00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:07.508
Oh, yeah? How do I do that?

82
00:05:07.575 --> 00:05:09.309
Start typing. See what happens.

83
00:05:09.376 --> 00:05:11.078
Tell you exactly
what's going to happen.

84
00:05:11.145 --> 00:05:13.981
I'm going to make one typo
and this typewriter

85
00:05:14.048 --> 00:05:16.184
is going straight
out the goddamn window.

86
00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.086
Maybe. Maybe. You'll like it.

87
00:05:19.153 --> 00:05:23.323
Who knows, maybe you're
the next Ernest Hemingway.

88
00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:26.093
[chuckles]

89
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.297
Yeah, I'm going to get
a cup of coffee
and get that window open.

90
00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.165
That's a start.

91
00:05:31.232 --> 00:05:34.334
[Bobby]
<i>They let me keep my badge,</i>
<i>but took my gun.</i>

92
00:05:34.401 --> 00:05:36.838
<i>I guess it was a smart move</i>
<i>or else my brains</i>

93
00:05:36.904 --> 00:05:39.472
<i>would be all over this</i>
<i>coffee machine right now.</i>

94
00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.442
Hey, you got a minute?

95
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:46.747
<i>I put the guy in the hospital.</i>
<i>And they put me behind a desk.</i>

96
00:05:48.783 --> 00:05:50.852
-[woman] <i>Pat to Baker's office.</i>
-[Rick] It's Rick.

97
00:05:50.918 --> 00:05:52.854
-How are you doing, Pam?
<i>-Good, Rick and you?</i>

98
00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.122
-Yeah, I'm okay.
<i>-What can I do for you?</i>

99
00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:56.489
Is the chief around?

100
00:05:56.557 --> 00:05:57.959
<i>Sure. Just hold a minute.</i>

101
00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:59.126
Okay. Thank you.

102
00:05:59.193 --> 00:06:00.828
You got till I get off hold.

103
00:06:00.895 --> 00:06:02.864
You need to give me
something more than paperwork

104
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.566
to keep me busy. I mean, I'm
losing my mind behind that desk.

105
00:06:05.633 --> 00:06:09.136
I really feel for you,
what you're going through
with Mary.

106
00:06:09.203 --> 00:06:13.406
It breaks my heart.
But my hands are tied.

107
00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:16.677
You're lucky that they're
allowing you in this building.

108
00:06:16.744 --> 00:06:18.613
Lucky. Rick, you got
to do something.

109
00:06:18.679 --> 00:06:21.182
First of all, it's captain.

110
00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:22.650
It's not Rick.

111
00:06:22.717 --> 00:06:25.186
Second of all,
I did do something.

112
00:06:25.253 --> 00:06:26.419
And you know what?

113
00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.688
That's why you're standing

114
00:06:27.755 --> 00:06:29.257
in my office and you're

115
00:06:29.323 --> 00:06:30.992
not standing
on an unemployment line.

116
00:06:31.058 --> 00:06:33.127
He was sleeping
with my wife, Rick.

117
00:06:33.194 --> 00:06:34.562
And what did you do?

118
00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:36.429
-You disfigured him?
-I broke his nose.

119
00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:39.466
Okay? Let's not get
too dramatic here.

120
00:06:39.533 --> 00:06:41.769
<i>-Captain Callahan?</i>
-Yes, Pam.

121
00:06:41.836 --> 00:06:43.871
<i>Can you hold for</i>
<i>a teensy bit longer?</i>

122
00:06:43.938 --> 00:06:48.142
Okay, sweetheart.
You have a teensy bit longer.

123
00:06:48.209 --> 00:06:50.745
Listen, I know. I just,

124
00:06:50.811 --> 00:06:53.648
sometimes I get
a bit of a hot head.

125
00:06:53.714 --> 00:06:56.350
Hot head?
You went fucking nuclear.

126
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.818
You should have seen him, Rick.
I mean,

127
00:06:57.885 --> 00:07:00.054
You should have just
walked out of there

128
00:07:00.121 --> 00:07:02.990
like I suggest that
you walk out of here now.

129
00:07:03.057 --> 00:07:08.129
I don't have time to
babysit your conscience.

130
00:07:08.195 --> 00:07:10.965
I'm under a lot of stress
with this department.

131
00:07:11.032 --> 00:07:12.967
<i>-Captain Callahan?</i>
-Yes.

132
00:07:13.034 --> 00:07:14.502
<i>I'm going to</i>
<i>put you through now.</i>

133
00:07:14.568 --> 00:07:16.737
Okay, thank you. Hold.

134
00:07:18.306 --> 00:07:21.509
Close the door behind you, okay?

135
00:07:21.575 --> 00:07:24.078
Hey, Captain Callahan.
Hi, sir. How you doing?

136
00:07:31.218 --> 00:07:33.955
<i>♪ Welcome back ♪</i>

137
00:07:34.021 --> 00:07:37.325
<i>♪ Welcome back, welcome back ♪</i>

138
00:07:37.391 --> 00:07:39.860
<i>♪ Welcome back ♪</i>

139
00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:48.369
[disco music playing]

140
00:07:48.436 --> 00:07:50.237
[sighs]

141
00:08:11.025 --> 00:08:13.160
[man 1] I told you, this was
some Grade-A shit.

142
00:08:13.227 --> 00:08:14.962
[man 2] It's great man,
some Grade-A shit.

143
00:08:15.029 --> 00:08:17.031
[man 1] You know what?
Fucking take it or leave it.

144
00:08:17.098 --> 00:08:19.100
[Bobby]
<i>In a situation like this,</i>

145
00:08:19.166 --> 00:08:23.237
<i>I'm required</i>
<i>to step in and regulate.</i>

146
00:08:23.304 --> 00:08:26.574
<i>But I was too drunk</i>
<i>to give a shit.</i>

147
00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:27.808
Cut you the--

148
00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.477
[Bobby] <i>Chris Rosenberg.</i>

149
00:08:29.543 --> 00:08:32.013
<i>He might have looked</i>
<i>like a dirtbag drug dealer</i>

150
00:08:32.079 --> 00:08:34.782
<i>mainly because that's</i>
<i>exactly what he was.</i>

151
00:08:34.849 --> 00:08:36.450
<i>He was pretty good at it, too.</i>

152
00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:39.553
<i>So good, in fact, that one day</i>
<i>someone noticed.</i>

153
00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.756
<i>Roy DeMeo.</i>

154
00:08:41.822 --> 00:08:44.058
<i>If the devil</i>
<i>decided to walk to Earth,</i>

155
00:08:44.125 --> 00:08:47.695
<i>he'd do it as Roy DeMeo</i>
<i>and no one would be the wiser.</i>

156
00:08:47.762 --> 00:08:49.730
<i>Roy loved his big brother,</i>
<i>Anthony.</i>

157
00:08:49.797 --> 00:08:52.233
<i>I mean, he fucking</i>
<i>idolized him.</i>

158
00:08:52.299 --> 00:08:55.504
<i>But Roy's life changed forever</i>
<i>in the spring of '51</i>

159
00:08:55.569 --> 00:09:00.007
<i>when Anthony came back</i>
<i>from Korea in a body bag.</i>

160
00:09:00.074 --> 00:09:02.143
<i>By the time</i>
<i>he was out of high school,</i>

161
00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:05.179
<i>Roy had a pretty good</i>
<i>loan shark and racket going.</i>

162
00:09:05.246 --> 00:09:07.815
<i>Business was good,</i>
<i>mainly because everyone</i>

163
00:09:07.882 --> 00:09:09.383
<i>knew not to mess with Roy.</i>

164
00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.052
<i>By the late '60s,</i>

165
00:09:11.118 --> 00:09:13.187
<i>Roy was running</i>
<i>with the Gambino family.</i>

166
00:09:13.254 --> 00:09:15.790
<i>Anthony Gaggi.</i>

167
00:09:15.856 --> 00:09:17.291
<i>Everybody called him Nino.</i>

168
00:09:17.358 --> 00:09:20.561
<i>He was a capo</i>
<i>in the Gambino family.</i>

169
00:09:20.628 --> 00:09:23.631
<i>Roy had his fingers</i>
<i>in everything</i>
<i>from loan sharking</i>

170
00:09:23.697 --> 00:09:25.833
<i>to grand theft auto</i>
<i>to drug dealing.</i>

171
00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.401
<i>The Gambinos frowned</i>
<i>upon the last one,</i>

172
00:09:27.468 --> 00:09:30.004
<i>but Roy became one</i>
<i>of their top earners.</i>

173
00:09:30.071 --> 00:09:33.074
<i>So they kept him</i>
<i>as their dirty little secret.</i>

174
00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.775
<i>Roy took Chris under his wing.</i>

175
00:09:34.842 --> 00:09:36.243
<i>He saw something in him.</i>

176
00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.846
<i>Chris became</i>
<i>Roy's right hand man.</i>

177
00:09:38.913 --> 00:09:40.614
<i>But that night,</i>
<i>I didn't know any of that.</i>

178
00:09:40.681 --> 00:09:43.651
<i>All I knew was some asshole</i>
<i>was about to get killed</i>

179
00:09:43.717 --> 00:09:46.020
<i>by another asshole.</i>

180
00:09:46.087 --> 00:09:50.257
<i>And in that moment,</i>
<i>something in the me just...</i>

181
00:09:50.324 --> 00:09:53.661
[shouts]

182
00:09:58.632 --> 00:10:02.036
[Bobby] <i>I took out</i>
<i>every raw deal I can dealt</i>
<i>in my life until then.</i>

183
00:10:02.103 --> 00:10:05.339
<i>Right into this poor</i>
<i>bastard's fucking face.</i>

184
00:10:05.406 --> 00:10:07.808
[punches continue]

185
00:10:14.682 --> 00:10:18.352
Ah, fuck, I didn't mean to...

186
00:10:19.687 --> 00:10:22.957
Thanks. You got a car?

187
00:10:25.793 --> 00:10:27.761
[chuckles]

188
00:10:27.828 --> 00:10:30.197
So, what do you do, Bobby?

189
00:10:30.264 --> 00:10:32.166
I'm an architect.

190
00:10:32.233 --> 00:10:35.604
Architect? You build
houses and shit?

191
00:10:35.669 --> 00:10:37.071
Yeah.

192
00:10:40.374 --> 00:10:42.042
Yeah, I don't buy it.

193
00:10:42.109 --> 00:10:44.579
You're just too shitty
to be an architect.

194
00:10:44.645 --> 00:10:47.982
Well, you know,
I'm a shitty architect.

195
00:10:48.048 --> 00:10:51.752
[laughs]

196
00:10:51.819 --> 00:10:53.387
-Thanks for the ride.
-Oh, yeah.

197
00:10:53.454 --> 00:10:56.390
And, uh, you know, thanks
for stepping in back there.

198
00:10:56.457 --> 00:10:59.160
Oh, yeah, don't mention it.

199
00:10:59.226 --> 00:11:01.662
Appreciate
if you didn't, either.

200
00:11:01.729 --> 00:11:03.532
Mum's the word.

201
00:11:03.598 --> 00:11:05.567
<i>You know...</i>

202
00:11:05.634 --> 00:11:07.034
Chris.

203
00:11:07.101 --> 00:11:08.669
[Bobby]
<i>...for a degenerate scumbag...</i>

204
00:11:08.736 --> 00:11:11.405
-I'll see you around.
-Yeah.

205
00:11:11.472 --> 00:11:14.341
<i>...this guy was all right.</i>

206
00:11:14.408 --> 00:11:16.710
[Chris] Mum's the word.

207
00:11:28.088 --> 00:11:30.525
[woman] It was a Cadillac. Gold.

208
00:11:30.592 --> 00:11:32.059
We just bought it.

209
00:11:32.126 --> 00:11:34.461
When you say gold,
you mean yellow?

210
00:11:34.529 --> 00:11:36.931
What difference does it make?
I saw the guy,

211
00:11:36.997 --> 00:11:39.066
he was about 5'9, 5'10.

212
00:11:39.133 --> 00:11:41.135
You know, that real
distinguished type, with the...

213
00:11:41.202 --> 00:11:43.938
-Ma'am. Ma'am.
-a mustache.

214
00:11:44.004 --> 00:11:46.675
Not trying to be rude,
but nine times out of ten

215
00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.475
you know what happens
when a car gets stolen?

216
00:11:48.543 --> 00:11:49.944
It stays stolen.

217
00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:51.712
Look, I'll take a report,
but I can't

218
00:11:51.779 --> 00:11:54.014
promise you any miracles.

219
00:11:54.081 --> 00:11:57.251
So what the fuck
am I paying taxes for?

220
00:12:04.725 --> 00:12:06.961
You ever hear
of the Gemini Lounge?

221
00:12:07.027 --> 00:12:09.564
The place on Flatlands?

222
00:12:09.631 --> 00:12:12.900
Yeah, it's a mob watering hole.

223
00:12:12.967 --> 00:12:15.436
You think any big fish
swim around in there?

224
00:12:15.503 --> 00:12:19.773
Big, small, probably
a couple of barracudas also.

225
00:12:51.171 --> 00:12:53.007
[Bobby] <i>I was looking at pieces</i>
<i>of a puzzle</i>

226
00:12:53.073 --> 00:12:54.942
<i>with no idea</i>
<i>how they fit together.</i>

227
00:12:55.009 --> 00:12:59.213
<i>But it was enough</i>
<i>to get me off my ass.</i>

228
